\ Test that type predicates compile and execute correctly in AOT mode.
\ type-of returns a type value; the = comparison on type values goes
\ through per-operation native fallback (not the fixnum/float fast path).
\ In AOT mode bail is fatal, so correct output proves the per-op
\ fallback handled type value comparison successfully.

classify: ( val -- ) [
  dup fixnum? [ drop "fixnum" print-line ] [
    dup float? [ drop "float" print-line ] [
      dup boolean? [ drop "boolean" print-line ] [
        dup string? [ drop "string" print-line ] [
          dup symbol? [ drop "symbol" print-line ] [
            drop "other" print-line
          ] if
        ] if
      ] if
    ] if
  ] if
] ;

\ Each call tests type-of followed by = on a type value.
42 classify
3.14 classify
t classify
f classify
"hello" classify
name: classify

\ Negative cases: verify correct classification when the type
\ does NOT match the first predicate tested.
"not a fixnum" classify
0.0 classify
